+stanza that triggered the error</li>
+          <li pn="section-8.3-2.2">has a 'type' attribute set to a value of &quot;error&quot;</li>
+          <li pn="section-8.3-2.3">typically swaps the 'from' and 'to' addresses of the generated
+stanza</li>
+          <li pn="section-8.3-2.4">mirrors the 'id' attribute (if any) of the generated stanza that
+triggered the error</li>
+          <li pn="section-8.3-2.5">contains an &lt;error/&gt; child element that specifies the error
+condition and therefore provides a hint regarding actions that the
+sender might be able to take in an effort to remedy the error
+(however, it is not always possible to remedy the error)</li>
         </ul>
